# minimum qore version
%requires qore >= 2.0
%requires xml
%requires WSDL
%requires Util
%requires Logger
%requires HttpClientIo
%requires(reexport) ConnectionProvider >= 1.4

%modern

module SoapClientIo {
    version = "1.0";
    desc = "SOAP client module with async I/O via HttpClientIo";
    author = "David Nichols <david@qore.org>";
    url = "http://qore.org";
    license = "MIT";
    init = sub () {
        ConnectionSchemeCache::registerScheme("soapio", SoapIoConnection::ConnectionScheme);
        ConnectionSchemeCache::registerScheme("soapios", SoapIoConnection::ConnectionScheme);
    };
}

/** @mainpage SoapClientIo Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section soapclientiointro Introduction to the SoapClientIo Module

    The %SoapClientIo module provides a SOAP client implementation using async I/O via
    \c HttpClientIo::HttpClientConnectionManager with automatic protocol negotiation
    (HTTP/3 &rarr; HTTP/2 &rarr; HTTP/1.1) and connection pooling.

    This module is the async I/O counterpart to the \c SoapClient module. It reuses the same
    \c WSDL web-service model, message serialization, envelope validation, node processing and
    fault grammar; only the transport differs. \c SoapClient remains available and unchanged for
    code that needs the synchronous \c HTTPClient API.

    To use this module, use \c "%requires SoapClientIo" in your code.

    All the public symbols in the module are defined in the SoapClientIo namespace.

    The module provides the following classes:
    - @ref SoapClientIo::SoapClientIo "SoapClientIo" - the main SOAP client class
    - @ref SoapClientIo::SoapIoConnection "SoapIoConnection" - connection provider for the
      ConnectionProvider framework

    @subsection soapclientio_features Features

    - SOAP 1.1 and SOAP 1.2 operations over async I/O with connection pooling and automatic
      protocol negotiation (HTTP/3 &rarr; HTTP/2 &rarr; HTTP/1.1)
    - The same WSDL model, request serialization, response decoding, envelope validation,
      mandatory-header processing and fault grammar as the \c SoapClient module
    - Native and retained XML response values, and portable type preservation
    - MTOM/XOP requests with the \c mtom option, also as a SoapIoConnection option, and MTOM/XOP response
      decoding
    - SOAP 1.2 envelope-free response retrieval with @ref SoapClientIo::SoapClientIo::getSoapResponse()
    - ConnectionProvider integration with \c soapio:// and \c soapios:// URL schemes

    @subsection soapclientio_usage Usage Example

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires SoapClientIo

SoapClientIo client({"wsdl": "http://example.com/service?wsdl"});
auto result = client.callOperation("echo", {"body": "invoice-71"});
printf("result: %N\n", result);
client.close();
    @endcode

    @section soapclientio_relnotes Release History

    @subsection soapclientio_v1_0 SoapClientIo v1.0
    - initial release providing SOAP 1.1 and SOAP 1.2 calls over async I/O
    - responses are parsed and decoded within @ref WSDL::SoapMessageLimits "SoapMessageLimits", selected by the
      \c message_limits option and SoapClientIo::setMessageLimits(), or otherwise by the calling thread or the WSDL
*/

#! the SoapClientIo namespace holds all public definitions in the SoapClientIo module
public namespace SoapClientIo {
}
